1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:16,305
Live browser • public API documentation
Fresh browser interactions, not a slideshow. Synthetic data only; this public demo uses
unencrypted HTTP.

2
00:00:16,305 --> 00:00:38,970
Live API • health check
Use Swagger Try it out and Execute. This sends a real request to the existing GKE
application.

3
00:00:38,970 --> 00:01:05,580
Live API • valid synthetic transaction
Paste five explicit strings. The API validates a request; it does not transfer money or
store balances.

4
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:25,705
Live API • Zero amount
Change only the amount to zero. This is a business-rule rejection: HTTP 200, valid false,
AMOUNT_NOT_POSITIVE.

5
00:01:25,705 --> 00:01:45,871
Live API • Same sender and recipient
Use the same opaque account identifier twice. The business rule rejects a self-transfer
request.

6
00:01:45,871 --> 00:02:06,124
Live API • Excess fractional precision
Use three fractional digits. The service rejects excess precision rather than silently
rounding money.

7
00:02:06,124 --> 00:02:26,255
Live API • Wrong input type
Send a JSON number instead of a decimal string. Strict boundary validation returns HTTP
422 without echoing the submitted value.

8
00:02:26,255 --> 00:02:46,377
Live API • Unknown request field
Add an undocumented field. Extra request fields are rejected; the public contract is not
silently expanded.

9
00:02:46,377 --> 00:03:06,511
Live API • Restore a valid request
Remove the extra field and restore the documented payload. The same running endpoint
accepts the valid request again.

10
00:03:06,511 --> 00:03:35,538
Reviewed source • exact API contract
Read the published contract: schema failures and business rejections are different.
Identifiers are case-sensitive; money uses Decimal.

11
00:03:35,538 --> 00:03:56,345
Reviewed source • pure business rules
HTTP handling and Pydantic schemas are separate from transaction rules. The service
performs no network or filesystem I/O.

12
00:03:56,345 --> 00:04:22,208
Reviewed source • container build and runtime
The Dockerfile builds a locked package and defines a non-root runtime. This source review
does not rebuild or execute a vulnerable artifact.

13
00:04:22,208 --> 00:04:50,043
Reviewed source • CI gate ordering
The Jenkinsfile places tests and security checks before image release. Actual retained
Jenkins results follow; no job is triggered for this recording.

14
00:04:50,043 --> 00:05:17,989
Historical Jenkins #39 • successful normal SCM run
This is the retained normal-main run, not a new execution. Navigate its real Jenkins
result and test report.

15
00:05:17,989 --> 00:05:42,405
Historical Jenkins #39 • pipeline steps
Review the actual native Pipeline Steps view. Separate stage observations from claims that
a build is running now.

16
00:05:42,405 --> 00:06:07,871
Historical Jenkins #39 • console and downstream trigger
The console records the SCM cause and successful upstream completion. Native triggering
started delivery #3.

17
00:06:07,871 --> 00:06:37,888
Historical delivery #3 • independent release worker
The native upstream cause identifies finsecure-ci #39. Reviewed release tools
independently verify the original candidate before credentials and mutation.

18
00:06:37,888 --> 00:06:57,888
Historical delivery #3 • actual deployed-image proof
Open the archived deployment report. It records owned Pods, image identity and successful
smoke checks. This is historical verification, not a new PATCH.

19
00:06:57,888 --> 00:07:21,445
Historical failure #37 • real failed-test block
One deliberate assertion failed in an isolated Replay. The fault did not change main, and
no downstream delivery followed.

20
00:07:21,445 --> 00:07:54,094
Historical failure #38 • image-security gate
The actual native scan summary records 38 HIGH and 2 CRITICAL findings. The scan
completed, but the gate withheld the image; it was never deployed.

21
00:07:54,094 --> 00:08:23,914
Historical operator rollback • verified result
Read the retained rollback record: one conditional PATCH, known-good 0.3.0, two Pods and
passing smoke. Rollback was explicit, not automatic.

22
00:08:23,914 --> 00:08:50,738
Live Grafana • cloud API observations
This dashboard queries the running local Prometheus observing GKE. Load-balancer sampling
is not complete per-Pod or reliable aggregate throughput.

23
00:08:50,738 --> 00:09:10,376
Historical alert • actual FIRING email
Open the retained cloud-scoped alert. The demonstration changed the scrape port, not the
application; no outage is induced during this recording.

24
00:09:10,376 --> 00:09:28,936
Historical alert • actual RESOLVED email
Port 80 was restored and scraping recovered. Mailpit proves local SMTP delivery, not
external email delivery.

25
00:09:28,936 --> 00:09:52,907
Historical cloud observations • native resource metrics
The reviewed GKE record contains separate CPU/memory observations for both nodes and
application Pods. Timestamps and original units remain visible.

26
00:09:52,907 --> 00:10:13,596
Historical Cloud Logging • sanitized event evidence
Actual centralized log observations retain only approved timestamps and validation events.
Private resource labels and request bodies are not shown.

27
00:10:13,596 --> 00:10:34,411
Architecture • current trust boundaries
Review the published architecture document: separate source execution, fixed release
authority, GKE runtime and locally hosted monitoring.

28
00:10:34,411 --> 00:10:58,081
AI triage • proposal only
No AI model is deployed. The proposal requires sanitized inputs, citations, bounded
outputs and human review; benefits are not measured results.

29
00:10:58,081 --> 00:11:15,667
Finish • evidence and access
Demonstration complete. Please refer to the repository, documentation and supporting
evidence for further details.
